report='''# R27 — native miniaudio backend, streaming and voice commands

GAME-EXE-EIREBUILD-ADDON-INTEGRATION-001 remains ACTIVE. All93 MOB registry handlers now have source implementations; GetSkill(tame) remains explicitly rejected, and this count is NOT full addon migration or gameplay equivalence.

Source work/eirebuild-local, branch/commit N/A copied engine snapshot. Read-only reference57b8e0c42061a0acd51eaf64ea008aa1447d94ee, feature/world-background-data-20260916. Reused unchanged installed-addon/source provenance from R19-R26. Exact touched files/reference hashes in r27-manifest.json; preimages in pre-r27. No addon source checkout edited, no live game files changed. No merge/push/publication. No new runtime toggle; only existing source settings/defaults read.

## Source changes
Imported the complete MiniaudioOneShotSfx implementation from the verified source:64 voice slots, encoded/decoded cache, PCM/MP3 decoder, virtual/managed lifetime, source spatialization, binaural/occlusion/reverb processing, scenario/party gain and speech duck envelope, streaming/markers, pause/cancel/device recovery and Bink backend code. Copied miniaudio.h, VoiceWaitState.h and ScenarioSpeechDucking.h byte-identically. The import itself does NOT make every API an engine callsite: Bink output is compiled but not connected yet.

Replaced retail CSoundManager/SFxControl offset literals with compiler-computed offsetof values using a narrow friend layout adapter; world, map and party accesses bind real native classes. Native party.people/nID and world.szZoneFileName map the source party.personages/id and MPR-name facade. No old EXE function addresses used for sound manager integration. Bink SDK lowercase numeric macros isolated around the unmodified third-party header. Reference LOG calls use OutputDebugString rather than importing the addon file logger; DeTest-only catalog activation is unavailable, explicit existing catalog setting remains. Diagnostic output parity is not claimed.

Native BeginFXInt flat/3D now routes mod sessions to virtual miniaudio voices; no legacy Miles fallback for these mod routes, matching the full-backend source policy. Native encoded RES reader supplies cached bytes with balanced CloseFile. Counter advances only after successful start, never wraps on reserved empty ID. PrepareNativeManager synchronizes manager/counter BEFORE capture so reset cannot erase a newly acquired cache entry. UpdateFX/CancelFX/IsFXValid/GetFXPlaybackTime, app pause/resume, StopAll and Destroy share the backend owner. Existing CSoundManager/Miles initialization still provides readiness; this is not removal of the MSS DLL dependency.

Streaming select/begin/end/current-name/volume/fade/pause hooks now call the imported music backend instead of the disabled native SM_SUPPORT_STREAMING path. Original marker enum values retained. Existing mod Stream override resolution is preserved in imported code. Modal/game pause selection uses actual interface screen depth and world combat pause, with original false defaults for both existing settings. Sound update applies these before the backend tick. Scenario speech has source half-volume envelope for other speech; other Audio.cpp music/category gain rules remain pending.

CreateVoiceFX387 and CreateVoiceFXWait390 validate living server speaker, resource/volume, paired finite radii and single-player ready sound manager. Party gain uses nearest living party XY distance and captured world/MPR identity without retaining NPC pointers. Wait uses the byte-identical atomic publication ticket and native thread sleep word; source backend publishes on actual successful sound start, releases on EOS/cancel/steal/reset. Synchronous loop depth is scoped/thread-local, with no new serialized member. Load clears pending negative ticket for replay of unfinished line, preserving ordinary native sleep values. Failure logs to native console and advances script. This preserves source failure-continuation intent; diagnostics differ from addon FunctionError plumbing.

CMappedResource mapped branch returned a data pointer without assigning directory length; now fills pnDataSize exactly like heap/cached paths, required for decoder capture. This narrow fix was source-inspected; the headless PCM fixture does not exercise a mapped RES view.

## Build and checks
Final Build82 ReleaseWin32 PASS. Build79 failed on Bink lowercase type macros conflicting with miniaudio member names; isolated macros fixed it. Build80 exposed native party member names, corrected to people/nID. Build81 and82 succeeded;82 contains streaming/pause/cache refinements and is the only delivered artifact. One headless run per successful changed artifact, no repeated checks on unchanged artifacts. PE32 x86/copy hashes and exact unchanged helper/library identities PASS.

Final r27-runtime.json: shared native stats/regeneration/MOB/parser/save round-trip checks PASS; voice Registry publish/capture/identity/stale-slot rejection, wait once/continue/failure, negative saved-ticket reset and preservation of positive native sleep, nested synchronous guard, no-manager start rejection without device creation, scenario duck attack/release/overlap PASS. Real miniaudio decoder captured a small in-memory PCM WAV, rejected invalid bytes, and cleared cache on Shutdown. These are decoder/lifetime-state tests, NOT audible playback or actual ma_sound EOS/pause/steal tests. No CSoundManager created by the new fixture, no audio device initialized, no game/UI/audio playback launched. No production3/3 claim.

## Remaining scope and confidence
Full parent NOT complete. Audio.cpp category priorities, dynamic resource/category gain resolver, pitch/volume variation, step variant logic, broader music ducking and Bink callsite connection are still pending. Current flat/3D adapter passes neutral1 gain/pitch; imported DSP algorithms are present but final mix parity is unproved until those source rules are connected. uRandomStartPosition legacy behavior is not forwarded by this adapter; compare source virtual route policy in the next audio block. Config Bink fields exist for imported code but do not imply the video engine uses it.

Gameplay remains deliberately deferred: real resource coverage, actual output/device recovery, full sound overlap/steal/EOS, pause menu and combat pause, party-distance gain across death/map changes, voicewait saved game and loops, streaming markers and codec compatibility, visual/rendering R17 defects. Also broader NPC equipment/spells, tactical AI/death fear/murder awareness/combat,16-slot/client/UI/network migration, notification presentation and tame semantics remain open. No claim that93 handlers or imported file size measures completion.

Exact next source step: adapt remaining Audio.cpp policy/gain/variation and Bink owner callsites against native engine objects, then return to remaining NPC/combat/UI parent inventory. After all source migration, manual acceptance should cover sequential/overlapping voice lines, wait end/cancel/steal, pause/resume, save/reload mid-line, party departure, music switch/loop and missing device. Do not launch before that phase per owner.

Clean package work/handoffs/eirebuild-x86-miniaudio-voice-20260916-r27 contains EXE/README/manifest; matching PDB separate in symbols/20260916-r27. Requires existing game dependencies/resources. Installed R8 and Starter route untouched. No permission for merge/push. Scope/assumptions/untested boundaries above remain material.
'''
